# Saved-record design evidence

The source snapshot records root HEAD
`6ab85278bea708337e20947966a54a5072ad0627` plus exact working file SHA-256 values,
including the then-uncommitted portable calculation boundary. No product files
were edited. No Astrofolio verification view or reserved trust work was used.

`probe.mjs` executes a freshly bundled copy of actual profile/account functions
against synthetic memory storage on Node 22.23.2. `result.json` records nine
controls: four passing boundary controls and five reproduced counterexamples.
Two of the latter are explicitly modeled proposals rather than product code.

Actual counterexamples: both real aggregate saves return `saved` while an allowed
interleaving loses one; a hypothetical new global key is absent from real
handoff inventory; account isolation and account-specific deletion succeed while
that key remains. Controls establish ordinary sequential saves, full prefix
clear, quota error reporting and A→B→A epoch rejection. The fixture uses synthetic
UUIDs, an unknown 2001-12-21 08:30 polar Placidus calculation and no real person.
No network calls occurred.

`native-idb-control.mjs` executes the actual frozen
`IndexedDbLivingChartAdapter` in Chrome 152.0.7977.83 native IndexedDB, through a
disposable browser context and an owned local HTTP server. It confirms atomic
capacity/CAS callbacks, proves that close does not abort an already active
transaction, and proves that upgrading the existing database to version 2 breaks
the current exact-version-1 adapter. The browser/context/server were closed.
Only synthetic disposable browser storage was changed.

These are bounded architecture probes, not acceptance of a new store or a claim
that current active profile behavior is fixed. The author task owns product
implementation, and this reviewer will separately review its frozen patch.

Initial bundle generation failed because the isolated source copy had no engine
or Supabase package resolution. The error is retained in
`initial-bundle-missing-dependencies.log`; the corrected bundle resolves existing
installed packages through an explicit Node search path. No dependency was
installed and no network behavior was invoked. The bundle input manifests and
exact emitted bytes are retained for reproducibility.
